diff --git a/docs/architecture/external-agent-protocol.md b/docs/architecture/external-agent-protocol.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e32885c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/architecture/external-agent-protocol.md
@@ -0,0 +1,250 @@
+# External Agent Plugin Protocol Specification
+
+## Overview
+
+The Entire CLI supports external agent plugins via executables discovered in `PATH`. This protocol allows third-party agent integrations without requiring modifications or re-compilation of the core Entire CLI repository.
+
+External agent plugins run as standalone binaries that communicate with Entire CLI via standard CLI subcommands using standard I/O streams (`stdin`, `stdout`, and `stderr`).
+
+---
+
+## Plugin Discovery & Lifecycle
+
+### Discovery
+Entire CLI scans the system `PATH` for executable binaries matching the pattern:
+```
+entire-agent-<name>
+```
+For example, `entire-agent-cursor` registers as an external agent named `cursor`.
+
+### Environment
+Every subcommand invocation runs in a stateless process with the following environment variables set:
+- `ENTIRE_REPO_ROOT`: Absolute path to the repository root directory.
+- `ENTIRE_PROTOCOL_VERSION`: Currently `1`.
+
+The current working directory (`cwd`) for plugin invocations is set to the repository root.
+
+### Error Handling
+- **Exit Code 0**: Success. Output (if required) is read from `stdout`.
+- **Non-zero Exit Code**: Failure. The error description should be printed to `stderr`. The CLI treats any non-zero exit code as an execution error.
+
+---
+
+## Capabilities
+
+An external agent declares its supported capabilities in its `info` subcommand response. Capabilities determine which subcommands the agent supports and which interfaces it implements in Entire CLI.
+
+```json
+{
+  "protocol_version": 1,
+  "name": "cursor",
+  "type": "Cursor",
+  "description": "Cursor - AI-powered code editor",
+  "is_preview": true,
+  "protected_dirs": [".cursor"],
+  "hook_names": ["session-start", "session-end", "stop"],
+  "capabilities": {
+    "hooks": true,
+    "transcript_analyzer": true,
+    "transcript_preparer": false,
+    "token_calculator": false,
+    "text_generator": false,
+    "hook_response_writer": false,
+    "subagent_aware_extractor": false
+  }
+}
+```
+
+---
+
+## Subcommand Reference
+
+### Core Subcommands (Required)
+
+#### `info`
+- **Requirement**: Always required.
+- **Description**: Returns metadata and declared capabilities for the agent.
+- **Input**: None
+- **Output (stdout)**: JSON object matching `InfoResponse` (see schema above).
+
+#### `detect`
+- **Requirement**: Always required.
+- **Description**: Checks whether the agent is installed/present in the environment.
+- **Input**: None
+- **Output (stdout)**: `{"present": true}` or `{"present": false}`
+
+#### `read-transcript --session-ref <path>`
+- **Requirement**: Always required.
+- **Description**: Reads the raw transcript bytes for a given session path/reference.
+- **Input**: None
+- **Output (stdout)**: Raw transcript bytes.
+
+#### `chunk-transcript --max-size <n>`
+- **Requirement**: Always required.
+- **Description**: Splits raw transcript data into chunks no larger than `<n>` bytes.
+- **Input (stdin)**: Raw transcript bytes.
+- **Output (stdout)**: JSON object:
+  ```json
+  {
+    "chunks": ["base64...", "base64..."]
+  }
+  ```
+
+#### `reassemble-transcript`
+- **Requirement**: Always required.
+- **Description**: Reassembles transcript chunks into raw bytes.
+- **Input (stdin)**: JSON object:
+  ```json
+  {
+    "chunks": ["base64...", "base64..."]
+  }
+  ```
+- **Output (stdout)**: Raw transcript bytes.
+
+#### `get-session-id`
+- **Requirement**: Always required.
+- **Description**: Extracts or computes the session ID from hook input data.
+- **Input (stdin)**: JSON `HookInput` object.
+- **Output (stdout)**: `{"session_id": "..."}`
+
+#### `get-session-dir --repo-path <p>`
+- **Requirement**: Always required.
+- **Description**: Returns the directory path where agent session files are stored for repository `<p>`.
+- **Input**: None
+- **Output (stdout)**: `{"session_dir": "..."}`
+
+#### `resolve-session-file --session-dir <d> --session-id <id>`
+- **Requirement**: Always required.
+- **Description**: Resolves the full path to a session file given session directory `<d>` and session ID `<id>`.
+- **Input**: None
+- **Output (stdout)**: `{"session_file": "..."}`
+
+#### `read-session`
+- **Requirement**: Always required.
+- **Description**: Parses hook input into an `AgentSession` object.
+- **Input (stdin)**: JSON `HookInput` object.
+- **Output (stdout)**: JSON `AgentSession` object.
+
+#### `write-session`
+- **Requirement**: Always required.
+- **Description**: Writes updated `AgentSession` data back to the agent session store.
+- **Input (stdin)**: JSON `AgentSession` object.
+- **Output**: None (exit 0 on success).
+
+#### `format-resume-command --session-id <id>`
+- **Requirement**: Always required.
+- **Description**: Returns the CLI command string used to resume the given session.
+- **Input**: None
+- **Output (stdout)**: `{"command": "..."}`
+
+---
+
+### Hook Operations (`capabilities.hooks = true`)
+
+#### `parse-hook --hook <name>`
+- **Requirement**: Required if `hooks = true`.
+- **Description**: Parses agent native hook payloads into normalized Entire `Event` objects.
+- **Input (stdin)**: Raw agent hook payload bytes.
+- **Output (stdout)**: JSON `Event` object or `null` if the hook payload does not generate a trackable event.
+
+#### `install-hooks [--local-dev] [--force]`
+- **Requirement**: Required if `hooks = true`.
+- **Description**: Installs native hooks for the agent into the environment/repo.
+- **Input**: None
+- **Output (stdout)**: `{"hooks_installed": 3}`
+
+#### `uninstall-hooks`
+- **Requirement**: Required if `hooks = true`.
+- **Description**: Uninstalls native hooks for the agent.
+- **Input**: None
+- **Output**: None (exit 0 on success).
+
+#### `are-hooks-installed`
+- **Requirement**: Required if `hooks = true`.
+- **Description**: Checks if native agent hooks are currently installed.
+- **Input**: None
+- **Output (stdout)**: `{"installed": true}` or `{"installed": false}`
+
+---
+
+### Transcript Analysis (`capabilities.transcript_analyzer = true`)
+
+#### `get-transcript-position --path <p>`
+- **Requirement**: Required if `transcript_analyzer = true`.
+- **Description**: Returns current byte offset or index position within the transcript file at `<p>`.
+- **Input**: None
+- **Output (stdout)**: `{"position": 1024}`
+
+#### `extract-modified-files --path <p> --offset <n>`
+- **Requirement**: Required if `transcript_analyzer = true`.
+- **Description**: Extracts list of files modified since byte offset `<n>` in transcript at `<p>`.
+- **Input**: None
+- **Output (stdout)**: JSON array of file path strings: `["src/main.go", "README.md"]`
+
+#### `extract-prompts --session-ref <p> --offset <n>`
+- **Requirement**: Required if `transcript_analyzer = true`.
+- **Description**: Extracts user prompts from transcript at `<p>` starting from offset `<n>`.
+- **Input**: None
+- **Output (stdout)**: JSON array of prompt objects.
+
+#### `extract-summary --session-ref <p>`
+- **Requirement**: Required if `transcript_analyzer = true`.
+- **Description**: Extracts a high-level summary of the session.
+- **Input**: None
+- **Output (stdout)**: `{"summary": "Implement feature X"}`
+
+---
+
+### Transcript Preparation (`capabilities.transcript_preparer = true`)
+
+#### `prepare-transcript --session-ref <p>`
+- **Requirement**: Required if `transcript_preparer = true`.
+- **Description**: Prepares/normalizes a transcript prior to checkpoint processing.
+- **Input**: None
+- **Output**: None (exit 0 on success).
+
+---
+
+### Token Calculation (`capabilities.token_calculator = true`)
+
+#### `calculate-tokens --offset <n>`
+- **Requirement**: Required if `token_calculator = true`.
+- **Description**: Calculates token usage for raw transcript input from offset `<n>`.
+- **Input (stdin)**: Raw transcript bytes.
+- **Output (stdout)**: JSON token usage object (`{"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 50}`).
+
+---
+
+### Text Generation (`capabilities.text_generator = true`)
+
+#### `generate-text --model <m>`
+- **Requirement**: Required if `text_generator = true`.
+- **Description**: Uses the agent model `<m>` to generate text from a prompt.
+- **Input (stdin)**: Prompt text string.
+- **Output (stdout)**: `{"text": "..."}`
+
+---
+
+### Hook Response Writer (`capabilities.hook_response_writer = true`)
+
+#### `write-hook-response --message <m>`
+- **Requirement**: Required if `hook_response_writer = true`.
+- **Description**: Writes a response in agent-native format for display or handling by the agent.
+- **Input**: None
+- **Output (stdout)**: Agent-native response format bytes.
+
+---
+
+### Subagent-Aware Extraction (`capabilities.subagent_aware_extractor = true`)
+
+#### `extract-all-modified-files --offset <n> --subagents-dir <d>`
+- **Requirement**: Required if `subagent_aware_extractor = true`.
+- **Description**: Extracts modified files including those modified by subagents in directory `<d>`.
+- **Input (stdin)**: Raw transcript bytes.
+- **Output (stdout)**: JSON array of modified file path strings.
+
+#### `calculate-total-tokens --offset <n> --subagents-dir <d>`
+- **Requirement**: Required if `subagent_aware_extractor = true`.
+- **Description**: Calculates total token usage including subagent tokens.
+- **Input (stdin)**: Raw transcript bytes.
+- **Output (stdout)**: JSON total token usage object.

